  "ExplanationCorrect": "Under uncertainty without probabilities, decision criteria reflect different attitudes toward risk. Maximax (optimistic): choose the strategy with the highest possible payoff across all states. Best payoffs: S1=$25M, S2=$18M, S3=$12M. Select S1 ($25M). Maximin (pessimistic): choose the strategy with the highest minimum payoff (best of the worst cases). Minimum payoffs: S1=−$5M, S2=$2M, S3=$6M. Select S3 ($6M). Minimax regret: compute the opportunity loss (regret) for each strategy in each state — the difference between the best possible payoff in that state and the strategy's payoff. Then select the strategy that minimizes the maximum regret. Regret table: Boom regrets: S1=$0, S2=$7M, S3=$13M. Normal regrets: S1=$2M, S2=$0, S3=$4M. Recession regrets: S1=$11M, S2=$4M, S3=$0. Maximum regret per strategy: S1=11, S2=7, S3=13. Minimax selects S2 (max regret = $7M). The three criteria give three different answers — maximax (S1, aggressive), maximin (S3, conservative), and minimax regret (S2, balanced) — illustrating that decision strategy depends on risk attitude.",
