  "ExplanationWrongC": "6,000 units comes from maximizing REVENUE rather than profit: MR = 0 → 60 − 0.01Q = 0 → Q = 6,000. Revenue peaks there, but profit does not — the 6,000th unit adds zero revenue while costing $20, so profit is already falling by that point. Profit maximization sets MR equal to MC ($20), not to zero.",
