  "DifficultyScore": 2,
  "ExplanationCorrect": "Throughput accounting ranks products by throughput per minute of the bottleneck. Throughput = selling price minus truly variable cost (direct materials). Product A: $300 − $120 = $180 over 30 minutes = $6.00 per minute. Product B: $200 − $60 = $140 over 20 minutes = $7.00 per minute. B generates $1.00 more throughput per bottleneck minute, so the scheduler should prioritize B at the constrained workstation. Per-unit throughput is misleading here: A has the higher unit throughput but consumes 50% more constraint time.",
