  "ExplanationCorrect": "EVPI = EV with perfect information − EV of the best act without it. EV of launching: (0.40 × $500,000) + (0.35 × $200,000) + (0.25 × −$150,000) = $200,000 + $70,000 − $37,500 = $232,500 (not launching is worth $0, so launching is best). With perfect information, the firm launches only when demand is high or medium: (0.40 × $500,000) + (0.35 × $200,000) + (0.25 × $0) = $270,000. EVPI = $270,000 − $232,500 = $37,500. Any market study costing more than $37,500 destroys value even if it were perfectly accurate — the ceiling for research spending.",
