   "ExplanationCorrect": "Differential (relevant) cost analysis: operating contributes $300K - $240K = $60K of margin, less $85K avoidable fixed = -$25K for the quarter. All-in quarter comparison on one baseline: operate = $300K - $240K - $85K avoidable - $60K unavoidable = -$85K; shut = -$60K unavoidable - $40K restart/recertification = -$100K. Operating therefore loses $85K versus $100K, better by $15K. Keep-or-drop theory requires counting ALL future avoidable outlays triggered by the decision, including restart penalties. Exam trap: stopping at 'margin below avoidable fixed, so shut it' and missing the restart cost that widens the shutdown loss.",
